Chapter: ColophonDogfood
  cites Colophon chapter Colophon
  cites Colophon chapter Impression
  cites Works chapter RepoProtocolPersist
  cites Works chapter KeyManager
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter ImportGate
  cites Foreword chapter Hamt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Kernel chapter AppPersist
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The first thing this repository ever stored, and an honest account of what
 happened.

 A quire goes in -- two chapters of it, signed, content-addressed, through the
 same import gate the compiler's quotation gate uses. Then one chapter is
 edited and stored again, which is the ordinary thing anybody does to a
 repository within five minutes of being handed one.

 What works, works completely: the bytes survive, the hashes address them, the
 gate admits them, a forged body is refused, and BOTH editions remain
 retrievable forever because a content-addressed store cannot lose a version it
 has been given -- it does not overwrite, it accumulates.

 What does not work is stated here rather than hidden, because a dogfood test
 that only prints its successes is a colophon: a claim the artefact makes about
 itself with no witness but itself.

   ASK FOR A CHAPTER BY NAME and the store cannot answer. There is no
   path-to-content index. app-scan-last returns the last fact OF KIND 30 --
   the last source file written, whichever chapter that happened to be -- so
   asking for Impression hands you Colophon. That gap is still open.

   ASK WHICH EDITION IS CURRENT and the store cannot answer. Both editions are
   present, both verify, and nothing on the disk says one supersedes the other.
   A store that cannot name the current version of a file is not yet source
   control, whatever else it is. That gap is still open too.

 The colophon in the quire we are storing can be checked, which is the joke and
 also the point: the book can tell you truthfully what it is. The library still
 cannot tell you where it is, or which one is the current one.

Section: The Quire We Are Going To Store

 Two chapters, standing in for the real files. The bodies contain a PIPE, which
 the old encoding would have cut them in half at, and newlines, which no
 single-sector fact could hold.

  colophon-body-v1 : Text
  colophon-body-v1 =
    "Chapter: Colophon\n"
    & "\n"
    & " The book describing its own making.\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Section: Definitions\n"
    & "\n"
    & "  Leaf =\n"
    & "   | Recto\n"
    & "   | Verso\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Page 1\n"

  colophon-body-v2 : Text
  colophon-body-v2 =
    "Chapter: Colophon\n"
    & "\n"
    & " The book describing its own making, corrected.\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Section: Definitions\n"
    & "\n"
    & "  Leaf =\n"
    & "   | Recto\n"
    & "   | Verso\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Page 1\n"

  impression-body : Text
  impression-body =
    "Chapter: Impression\n"
    & "\n"
    & " One printing of a work.\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Page 1\n"

Section: Helpers

  press-keypair : Keypair
  press-keypair = generate-keypair (sha256 (text-to-bytes "the-colophon-press"))

  outcome-name : ImportOutcome -> Text
  outcome-name (o) =
    when o
      is ImportOk (f) -> "ImportOk"
      is ImportMissing -> "ImportMissing"
      is ImportCorrupt -> "ImportCorrupt"
      is ImportUnsigned -> "ImportUnsigned"
      is ImportUnknownSigner -> "ImportUnknownSigner"
      is ImportForged -> "ImportForged"
      is ImportUntrusted (s) -> "ImportUntrusted"

  chapter-of : Maybe Fact -> Text
  chapter-of (m) =
    when m
      is Just (f) -> first-line (f.content) 0 (text-length (f.content)) ""
      is None -> "not found"

  admitted-line : ImportResult -> Text
  admitted-line (r) =
    when r.outcome
      is ImportOk (f) -> first-line (f.content) 0 (text-length (f.content)) ""
      is otherwise -> "REFUSED"

  first-work : Work
  first-work = Work { w-title = "Colophon", w-body = colophon-body-v1 }

  def-line : Maybe SourceDefinition -> Text
  def-line (m) =
    when m
      is Just (d) -> (d.sd-chapter) & ", " & show (text-length (d.sd-content)) & " bytes"
      is None -> "not found"

  current-line : WorkIndex, Text -> Text
  current-line (ix) (path) = def-line (work-current ix path)

  hash-line : WorkIndex, Text -> Text
  hash-line (ix) (h) = def-line (work-by-hash ix h)

  current-hash : WorkIndex, Text -> Text
  current-hash (ix) (path) =
    when work-current ix path
      is Just (d) -> d.sd-hash
      is None -> ""

  tree-line : WorkIndex, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  tree-line (ix) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else let p = list-at (work-tree ix) i
    in tree-line ix (i + 1) len (if i == 0 then p else acc & "  |  " & p)

 What the store hands back when you ask by name. It has no way to take a name,
 so it takes the kind, and the answer is whichever chapter was written last.

  scanned-chapter : DiskFactStore -> Text
  scanned-chapter (store) =
    when app-scan-last store persist-kind-definition
      is None -> "nothing"
      is Just (line) ->
        when source-def-from-text line
          is None -> "an unparseable record"
          is Just (d) -> d.sd-chapter & " (the last one written)"

  first-line : Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  first-line (s) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else if char-code (char-at s i) == newline-code then acc
    else first-line s (i + 1) len (acc & char-to-text (char-at s i))

  newline-code : Integer = char-code (char-at "\n" 0)

  unsigned-def : Text, Text, Text -> SourceDefinition
  unsigned-def (path) (chapter) (body) =
    SourceDefinition {
      sd-hash = "",
      sd-path = path,
      sd-quire = "Colophon",
      sd-chapter = chapter,
      sd-signer = "",
      sd-signature = [],
      sd-author = "",
      sd-timestamp = 0,
      sd-content = body
    }

Section: Entry

  opening : [Device.Block, Console.Write] Nothing = act
    let kp = press-keypair
    in let manifest = manifest-add manifest-empty (kp.fingerprint) (kp.public-key) 100
    in let c1 = sign-definition kp (unsigned-def "apps/colophon/Colophon.codex" "Colophon" colophon-body-v1) 1700000001
    in let im = sign-definition kp (unsigned-def "apps/colophon/Impression.codex" "Impression" impression-body) 1700000002
    in let c2 = sign-definition kp (unsigned-def "apps/colophon/Colophon.codex" "Colophon" colophon-body-v2) 1700000003
    in let s0 = disk-init
    in let s1 = repo-persist-save-definition s0 c1 1700000001
    in let s2 = repo-persist-save-definition s1 im 1700000002
    in let s3 = repo-persist-save-definition s2 c2 1700000003
    in act
      print-line-uni "-- the quire goes in --"
      let store = disk-load
      in let bundle = repo-bundle-from-disk store
      in act
        print-line-uni ("chapters stored: " & show (list-length (repo-persist-load-all-definitions store)))
        print-line-uni ("Colophon, first edition:  " & outcome-name ((gate-import bundle manifest 50 (c1.sd-hash) "Colophon").outcome))
        print-line-uni ("Impression:               " & outcome-name ((gate-import bundle manifest 50 (im.sd-hash) "Impression").outcome))
        print-line-uni ("Colophon, second edition: " & outcome-name ((gate-import bundle manifest 50 (c2.sd-hash) "Colophon").outcome))

        print-line-uni ""
        print-line-uni "-- the colophon can be checked, which is new --"
        let w = Work { w-title = "Colophon", w-body = colophon-body-v1 }
        in let imp = Impression { imp-number = 1, imp-when = 1700000001, imp-printer = kp.fingerprint }
        in let note = colophon-of w imp
        in act
          print-line-uni ("the note names the hash the store filed it under: " & (if colophon-holds w note then "yes" else "NO"))
          print-line-uni ("and the store agrees:                             " & (if colophon-hash w == c1.sd-hash then "yes" else "NO"))
          print-line-uni ("that same note about the SECOND edition:          " & (if colophon-holds (Work { w-title = "Colophon", w-body = colophon-body-v2 }) note then "ACCEPTED -- WRONG" else "refused"))
        end

        print-line-uni ""
        print-line-uni "-- both editions are still here, and both verify --"
        print-line-uni ("  first:  " & admitted-line (gate-import bundle manifest 50 (c1.sd-hash) "Colophon"))
        print-line-uni ("  second: " & admitted-line (gate-import bundle manifest 50 (c2.sd-hash) "Colophon"))
        print-line-uni "A content-addressed store cannot lose an edition. It does not overwrite; it"
        print-line-uni "accumulates, and every edition it was ever given is still exactly itself."
        print-line-uni ""
        print-line-uni "-- ask the KERNEL for a chapter by name, and it answers the wrong question --"
        print-line-uni "app-scan-last takes a KIND, not a name, so it hands back the last fact of kind"
        print-line-uni "30 -- the last source file written, whichever chapter that happened to be."
        print-line-uni ("  asked for Impression, the kernel offers: " & scanned-chapter store)
        print-line-uni "It does not fail. It answers a question nobody asked, which is worse. And"
        print-line-uni "DiskFacts' own index cannot help: disk-load keys each fact by the hash of the"
        print-line-uni "stored LINE, not of the content that line describes, so a source body cannot"
        print-line-uni "be found by its own content hash at all."
        print-line-uni ("  disk-read-fact, by the body's true hash: " & chapter-of (disk-read-fact store (c1.sd-hash)))
        print-line-uni "That is an index of records. A repository needs an index of works."

        print-line-uni ""
        print-line-uni "-- so here is one --"
        let ix = repo-index-from-disk store
        in act
          print-line-uni ("the tree: " & show (list-length (work-tree ix)) & " works")
          print-line-uni ("  " & tree-line ix 0 (list-length (work-tree ix)) "")
          print-line-uni ""
          print-line-uni "ask it BY NAME and it answers the question you asked:"
          print-line-uni ("  apps/colophon/Impression.codex -> " & current-line ix "apps/colophon/Impression.codex")
          print-line-uni ("  apps/colophon/Colophon.codex   -> " & current-line ix "apps/colophon/Colophon.codex")
          print-line-uni ""
          print-line-uni "and the current Colophon is the SECOND edition, because the last write for a"
          print-line-uni "path is the current value of that path. That is what a log has always meant,"
          print-line-uni "and it needs no supersession record to say it:"
          print-line-uni ("  current == the second edition: " & (if current-hash ix "apps/colophon/Colophon.codex" == c2.sd-hash then "yes" else "NO"))
          print-line-uni ""
          print-line-uni "SUPERSEDING IS NOT DELETING. The first edition is still here, still verifies,"
          print-line-uni "and always will. It is simply no longer what the path points at:"
          print-line-uni ("  the first edition, fetched by its hash: " & hash-line ix (c1.sd-hash))
          print-line-uni ("  and it still hashes to itself:          " & (if colophon-hash first-work == c1.sd-hash then "yes" else "NO"))
        end

        print-line-uni ""
        print-line-uni "-- what is still missing --"
        print-line-uni "There is no way to say a path is GONE. A tombstone, and the removal it would"
        print-line-uni "let you express, is 6.5. Until then this store can add and it can revise, and"
        print-line-uni "it cannot forget -- which, for a repository, is the right way round to be"
        print-line-uni "incomplete."
      end
    end
  end

Page 1
